## 7. MOROCCO'S AEROSPACE INDUSTRIAL BASE

### 7.1 Quantitative Assessment

Morocco's aerospace sector is Africa's largest and the Mediterranean's fastest-growing, measured by export revenue and compound annual growth rate. The following data are drawn from Moroccan government and industry reporting.

Aerospace export revenues grew from under $100 million in 2004 to a record $2.64 billion in 2024 — a 26-fold increase over two decades — averaging approximately 13% compound annual growth. In the first half of 2025, exports reached $1.41 billion, up 8.8% year-on-year. [Morocco World News](https://www.moroccoworldnews.com/2025/10/263514/morocco-joins-elite-circle-of-aircraft-engine-manufacturing-nations/) More than 150 aerospace companies are currently operating in Morocco, generating $2.6–$3 billion in annual exports. The country has established itself as Africa's top aerospace manufacturing hub. [The North Africa Post](https://northafricapost.com/97206-morocco-emerges-as-mediterranean-fastest-aerospace-manufacturing-hub.html)

In terms of industrial tier, Morocco joined the elite circle of aircraft engine manufacturing nations, one of only five countries globally with this production capability. [Morocco World News](https://www.moroccoworldnews.com/2025/10/263514/morocco-joins-elite-circle-of-aircraft-engine-manufacturing-nations/) Pratt & Whitney opened a Casablanca engine manufacturing facility in April 2026. Safran operates engine repair facilities processing Boeing 737 and Airbus A320 engines. Boeing deepens component manufacturing annually. Lockheed Martin conducted site visits in December 2024 with exploration of partnership structures. The sector has adopted additive manufacturing for complex component production, IoT-integrated process digitalisation, and advanced composite materials innovation, contributing to international projects developing equipment for hydrogen-powered aircraft. [Industrie du Maroc](https://industries.ma/en/the-aerospace-industry-in-2024-a-moroccan-success-story-inspiring-the-world/)

